          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.537,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Division with a Decimal Divisor"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.115,
            0.846,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 12:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ravi went from Pune to Matheran by scooter in 2.5 hours. The distance was 126 km. What was his average speed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.16,
            0.847,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can get the average speed by dividing the distance by the time taken."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.198,
            0.246,
            0.216
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "1 2 6 \\div 2 . 5 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.221,
            0.842,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the divisor is a decimal, we convert the divisor into a fraction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.246,
            0.419,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "126 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{25}{10}=126\\times\\frac{10}{25}=\\frac{1260}{25}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.286,
            0.749,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "With the long division procedure we find the quotient is 50.4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.31,
            0.809,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the average speed at which Ravi travelled was 50.4 km per hour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.344,
            0.431,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 13: Find 4.68 ÷ 1.3."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.37,
            0.643,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Again converting the divisor into a fraction we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.4,
            0.417,
            0.437
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "4.68 \\div \\frac{13}{10} = 4.68 \\times \\frac{10}{13} = \\frac{46.8}{13}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.44,
            0.439,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, what about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4.68 \\div 0.13?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.469,
            0.563,
            0.507
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "4.68 \\div 0.13 = 4.68 \\div \\frac{13}{100} = 4.68 \\times \\frac{100}{13} = \\frac{468}{13}"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.518,
            0.494,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you notice in these cases?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.551,
            0.847,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the divisor is a decimal, we can convert it into a counting number by suitably multiplying it by 10, 100, 1000, and so on. We must also multiply the dividend by the same number. Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.382,
            0.613,
            0.615,
            0.651
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{4.68}{0.13} = \\frac{4.68 \\times 100}{0.13 \\times 100} = \\frac{468}{13}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.654,
            0.846,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Once we convert the divisor into a counting number, we can then follow the division using place value procedure to find the quotient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.711,
            0.402,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does This Ever End?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.735,
            0.715,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Can you calculate 10 ÷ 3? Try dividing using long division."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.762,
            0.374,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10 1 Tens + 0 Ones."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.786,
            0.846,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Regroup 1 Tens into 10 Ones. 10 Ones ÷ 3 3 Ones, and 1 Ones remain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.829,
            0.846,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Regroup 1 Ones as 10 Tenths. 10 Tenths ÷ 3 3 Tenths, and 1 Tenths remain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "84"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
